    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d54">

                <pb facs="0034" n="28" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg28"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111 A.R./350½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Chief of the Division
                        of European Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Moffat</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-09-25">September 25, 1939</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In the course of a conversation this morning Mr. Hoyer Millar<anchor n="22"
                        xml:id="d54-f1"/> told me that according to a report from the British
                    Minister at Panama, <pb facs="0035" n="29" xml:id="pg29"/> the German Minister
                    had asked for permission to have a German delegation present at the conference
                    as “observers”. The Panamanian Minister of Foreign Affairs declined the
                    suggestion.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Pierrepont Moffat</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d54-f1" n="22" xml:id="d54-f1-content">
                <p>F. R. Hoyer Millar, First Secretary of the British Embassy.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
